j2(a){switch(a){case"Show me Nvidia":return"You can tap here to view #NVDA"
case u.N:return"Often just buying the SP500 is a great option, it diversifies your positions across the whole stock market, and is much less risky than stock picking.\n\nIf you saved $10 a day for 20 years, you would have $70,000, but if you invested those same $10 in the SP500, you would now have around $4 millions\n\n"
case"Why is the SP500 such a good trade?":return"The SP500 represents the economy itself, and since the government wants the economy to do well, they manipulate its price by printing money and adjusting interest rates to boost the economy.\n\nThey stimulate spendings and create inflation to boost the sp500, it is the essence of how our economy works.\n\nThe SP500 (symbol SPY) can fluctuate in the short term, but over the long run, it will always increase.\n\n"
case"How to know a stock Analyst's price Forecast?":return"From the stock financial data screen, tap the 'More' button to see its financial data details and access its Analyst's price forecast.\n\n\nYou can also ask me: 'Apple price forecast' or '#AAPL price forecast'"
case"How to look for market Trends?":return"You can look for market trends from the Portfolio Analysis button.\n\nCheck the ETF tab and play with the selected time Period to look at the market trends per sectors."
case"How to look for Short Term Gains?":return"You want to find a stock which price might rocket soon? Look at the upcoming Earnings Announcements in the Screener here\n\n\nYou can also ask me: 'This week earnings'.\n\n"
case"How to trade with Virtual Money?":return"To trade virtual money in the app, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the app and navigate to the trading section.\n2. Select the stock or asset you want to trade.\n3. Choose the type of trade you want to execute, such as buying or selling.\n4. Enter the quantity or amount you want to trade.\n5. Review the trade details and confirm the transaction.\n6. Monitor your trades and track their performance in your portfolio.\n\nPlease note that trading with virtual money in the app is for educational and practice purposes only. It does not involve real money or real trading."
case"How to look for Long Term Gains?":return"You want to find a stock that will grow exponentially? Ask me: 'What are the stocks that impacted the market this week?'\n\n"
case u.A:return"You know what you want, but maybe there is better: You're thinking of buying Tesla / any other company for long term gains? First check in our Analytics if any of its competitors is a better deal!\n\nYou can click on the Competition button (top right) to compare Tesla with its competitors over time here.\n\n\nAnd don't forget to ask the community! Human Financial Advisors will help you for free! They want followers.\n\n"
case"How to Find the next Short Squeeze?":return"A short squeeze happens when the price of a highly shorted stock goes up, thus forcing short sellers to buy the stock back in quantities that impact the market price.\n\nThe stock price can do x1000 in a week... If the stock rallies and people start buying them, short sellers will need to close their positions to stop losses, and the price will do x1000\n\nThis is what happened to GameStop! \n\nYou can find the next short squeeze by sorting companies by Short Interest Ratio in the Screener here."
case"How to Find the best Shorts?":return"You can find the stocks with high short interest compared to current trading volume by looking at companies with high Short Interest Ratio in the Screener here."
case"What Cryptos are Trending?":return"You will find cryptos with anomalies in trading volumes (incredibly high) compared to average here.\n\nYou can also find Cryptos Social Scores in the Screener here.\n\n\n"
case"Which Stocks will See Price Changes Soon?":return"You can find companies with upcoming Price Moves by looking at the upcoming Earnings Announcements in the Screener here.\n\n\nAn earnings announcement is an official public statement of a company's profitability for a specific period, typically a quarter or a year.\n\nIf a company has been profitable, its share price will increase after its earnings are released."
case"How can I diversify my Portfolio?":return"Diversifying your portfolio means spreading your investments across different Asset Classes (Stocks, Cryptos etc.), Industries (Tech, HealthCare etc.), and Geographic Regions to reduce overall risk.\n\nA great and simple Strategy is to buy the Company with the Highest Valuation When Investing, it is the first company in the Screener here.\n\n\nSelect the Filter Icon on the Top Right Corner and Filter on 'Sectors' One By One, then Buy the Stock with the Highest Market Valuation for Each Sector!\n\n"
case u.aF:return"You can find companies that Pays the Highest Dividends by Sorting on the Dividend Yield metric in the Screener here.\n\n\nYou will find Energy and Real Estate companies that pay 25% Dividend Yield, that's $25 per $100 invested!\n\n\n\nYou can also Tap here to view the constituents and performance of BlackRock Ultra high paying dividend stocks ETF #HDV \n\n\nYou can sort by contribution to find the stocks with highest contribution to performance of the ETF."
case"What is the Market?":return"The stock market is often referred as 'the market'. The S&P 500 index helps us understand how the overall stock market is performing: it shows how the biggest US companies' stocks are doing.\n\nIf you had saved $10 a day and invested it in the SP500, for 20 years, you would now have around $5 millions\n\nOften just buying the SPY is a great option, it diversifies your positions across the whole stock market.\n\nYou can buy the Market here, by taping on this message to access the symbol SPX.\n\n\nIn Practice, only 5% of Investors manage to beat the market: Warren Buffett being the most famous of all!\n\n"
case"What are the Stocks with the Highest Price Moves?":return"Beta is a financial metric that tells you which Stocks have the highest Price Moves! Be aware: these are also the most risky Stocks!\n\nA beta value that is less than 1.0 means that the security is less volatile than the market (SP500). Including this stock in a portfolio makes it less risky than the same portfolio without the stock.\n\nYou can find companies with Highest Price Moves by looking at the Beta financial metric in the Screener here."
case"When To Sell?":return"The decision depends on market conditions and news.\n\nIf negative news are forecasted and market price keeps dropping, I will recommend you to stop losses.\n\nThe decision also depends on your portfolio weights.\n\nFor instance, if a stock performs overly well and becomes the main performance driver of your portfolio, you should rebalance risks across other alternatives.\n\nBuy the stocks / crypto in your virtual portfolio below and I will tell you when to sell."
case"How to assess my skills?":return"First add virtual holdings in StocksToBuyNow trading tool.\n\nYou will know how to beat the SP500 once you have at least 8 stocks / crypto in your virtual portfolio.\n\nYou will receive your selection, allocation and interaction skills values.\n\nHave a look at the mathematics of attribution, please share the link to your social media for support."
default:return""}},
